//// rakun-starter-web — a starter: a curated dependency set, and no code.
////
//// Declaring it pulls `rakun-starter` and `rakun-web` (the middleware chain, content negotiation, problem details); validation is the bundled library `validation`, reached with `from "validation"` and never listed. An application keeps importing from the modules
//// themselves (`from "rakun-web"`, `from "rakun-cache"`, …); nothing is
//// importable from the starter, so a starter can drop a module without
//// breaking an import. The versions are `rakun/version_set`'s.
